{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.PermLength"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mem_ascending_or_image_subgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mem_ascending_or_image_subgroup","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L167-L180","doc":"**The pairing, on a subgroup.**  Every element is length-ascending under\n`mulSwap i` or the image of one that is — with no closure hypothesis, since a\nsubgroup containing `sᵢ` supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mem'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mem'","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L160-L165","doc":"The same, phrased with the simple reflection `s n i` of the Coxeter system,\nwhich is how a Young subgroup is presented. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mem","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L154-L158","doc":"A subgroup containing `sᵢ` is closed under `mulSwap i` — by `mul_mem`, and\nnothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mem_ascending_or_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mem_ascending_or_image","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L131-L144","doc":"**The ascending half determines the set.**  Every element of a closed `S` is\neither length-ascending under `mulSwap i` or the image of one that is — the split\nthe Murphy pairing sums over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_bij","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_bij","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L121-L129","doc":"On a set closed under `mulSwap i`, the map is a bijection of the set onto\nitself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_ne","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The two are never the same length — a corollary worth having on its own, since\nit is what makes \"one goes up, the other down\" a genuine split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_cases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_cases","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L101-L107","doc":"The dichotomy as a plain disjunction, when only the lengths are wanted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.length_swap_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L73-L99","doc":"**Exactly one of `w` and `w·sᵢ` is longer, and by exactly one.**\n\nThis is the fact the Murphy-element pairing argument turns on: for each `w`, one\nof the two `rsFun` branches applies to `w` and the other to `w·sᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_ne","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L63-L69","doc":"**`mulSwap` has no fixed point**: `w ≠ w·sᵢ`, so the pairing is genuine. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_apply_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_apply_succ","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L59-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_apply_castSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_apply_castSucc","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The two values `sᵢ` exchanges, read off through `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_injective","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L51-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mulSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap_mulSwap","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L43-L46","doc":"`mulSwap i` is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ParabolicPairing.mulSwap","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ParabolicPairing.lean#L39-L41","doc":"Right multiplication by the simple reflection `sᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}